# Testing

Source of truth: `docs/development.md`, `docs/api-contract.md`, `README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Use existing `tests/` as the pattern.

## MUST

- Add or update tests when financial behavior changes
- Keep calculation functions independently testable (no I/O required to unit-test formulas)
- Add or update API/contract tests when API behavior changes
- Where practical, cover architectural boundary expectations in tests
- Preserve existing tests unless the intended behavior is deliberately changing and that change is documented

## Prefer covering

- Normal cases
- Zero values
- Missing inputs (`needs_input` with `{field, unit}`)
- Invalid inputs
- Boundary conditions
- Financial invariants
- Scenario behavior when scenarios are introduced (not required until scenarios exist)

## MUST NOT

- Impose heavy testing ceremony (no mandated coverage %, no new frameworks beyond pytest already in use)
- Delete or weaken tests solely to make a change pass
